gpui: Report the blur of a focused field the app takes out of the tree

Against longbridge/nsh e626a8d (0.4.0). A focused field removed from the
tree lost its focus quietly (text_input::focused clears it without an
event). A RichEditor binds every editing key (keys::key_table, When::Always)
while its hidden input reports focus, and lets go only on the blur; when
the app removes a focused editor and keeps a ref to it, the component is
not released, the blur never comes, and its bindings stay in the
surface's table, newest first, so every plain Input loses Backspace,
Delete, the arrows, Home/End, Enter, Tab and Escape. After each batch, a
focused field that is no longer attached now reports its blur.
Repro: workspace/hostfix/h2.tsx + h2.test.tsx, `nsh test h2.test.tsx
--target gpui` (fails on e626a8d, passes with this patch).

